Loglan started out without capitals and periods, but there were so many 
complaints
that JCB eventually came round to the idea, and introduced other 
unspoken punctuation.
However, he expected that there would be a 'resolver' that would be 
able to reconstruct
a sentence from a spoken sentence, that would be able to reconstruct 
the canonical
written form exactly.  This was largely achieved, apart from a problem 
with spoken
acronyms, for which I had offered a solution which he did not wish to 
accept.

